> You're assuming that you won't get cheated by the shop keeper? Why?
> What about other items damaging potions and scrolls while you're
> moving the cart around?

I probably didn't make this clear enough, but items would only be
damaged when you tried to #ride it, not as a constant chance of stuff
breaking. That would be silly.

> And the possibility of creatures grabbing something from the cart would
> need to be added to the code of course. They don't need intelligence to
> get something, they just grab what they can see - everything.

Funnily enough, this is one of the few occasions I agree with you,
APLer. But remember, monsters don't pick up ALL objects they see, do
they? And considering you're right next to the cart, anything that
tried to steal your groceries would most likely end up with a large
headache, possibly a missing limb, as opposed to a few free goodies.

> With the risk of falling off when you initially got on, going through a
> doorway A falling rock trap. Even water traps might change things. Down
> staircases *would* be decended with an increased chance of falling off.
> Hitting an up staircase would ensure you would fall off. This brings up
> the further possibility: the leash for the cart causing *more* damage
> when you fall off. The idea of a skill seems to have been created as well.

Yeah, a lot of interesting ideas. I'm thinking the (c)lose command is
probably the best way of attaching it to oneself (when I mentioned a
cross between a container and a leash, I didn't _actually_ mean a
leash was attached to it). You'd be able to do it while wielding a
weapon, and I think a restriction on having a hand free would make
sense (as in, no #twoweapon or two-handed weapons plus the cart; only
one or the other).

An important question is this: how much would it weigh?

In regards to all your various suggestions, I'll address them in
order:
 a) Going through a doorway wouldn't be that hard. Remember, NHINRL.
And you're an adventurer. That calls for some amazing feats, doesn't
it?
 b) Falling rock traps would hit you, then fall in the cart. I don't
think a single rock could shatter a potion, even if it _did_ bounce
off your head.
 c) I'm not sure if I like the idea of a "thoroughly rusted shopping
cart named Main" (i.e. what impact would it have on gameplay? Giants
can't hit for as much damage while wielding it?), but I don't see
what's wrong with it either. It'd be a nice touch.
 d) Sure, going down stairs would be dangerous in a shopping cart.
Sure, popular culture has an obnoxious liking of repetetive 4-chord
music. But just _falling off_ the cart would be boring, and would kill
the point of having one. I mean, it's like "Damn, I just fell off for
the 20th time. Yay, now I need to see if that last potion will break
when I hop in. The last of fifty holy waters."
 e) What would a seperate riding skill actually achieve? I don't
really think it's necessary.

Otherwise, although I find many of your postings to be a complete
waste of time, I thank you for having the decency to make this one
relatively intelligent.


